# Round 51 — Hilbert–Pólya candidates 2.0: the missing property is always the whole problem

| construction | missing property | gap ≡ RH? | verdict |
|--------------|------------------|-----------|---------|
| Berry–Keating xp, Sierra regularizations | self-adjoint realization with spectrum exactly the zeros | unknown | open (no route) |
| Bender–Brody–Müller 2017 | self-adjointness on the right domain, completeness | unknown | CIRCULAR |
| Connes 1999 absorption spectrum | trace-formula positivity | reduces to Weil positivity | open (no route) |
| Yakaboylu 2024–25 | the similarity transform's positivity | yes | CIRCULAR |
| LeClair–Mussardo 2024 | unitarity of the scattering picture | yes | CIRCULAR |
| Remmen 2021 amplitude | completeness / positivity of residues | unknown | CIRCULAR |
| de Branges / canonical systems for ξ | Hermite–Biehler property | yes | CIRCULAR |
| Okubo, Castro–Mahecha, Wu–Sprung | rigorous operator; numerics only | unknown | open (no route) |

Every candidate delivers either an operator without a proof that its spectrum is exactly the zeros, or such
an identification with a self-adjointness/positivity condition that is itself equivalent to RH.
